MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me combines Christmas music with vocal harmonies, making it the strongest connection to my repeated holiday listening and interest in The New Old Fashioned.",
    "To Be Loved and Partners have some appeal through familiar vocals and duets, although that connection is weaker than Christmas music with group harmonies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Fleetwood Mac, Eagles, and Lesley Gore collections do not connect to the seasonal music or vocal harmonies I want enough to make me choose them.",
    "Adele and Carole King may appeal as singers, but that alone does not satisfy my current interest; Storyteller gives me too little indication of a closer match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to treat a broad interest in familiar singers as enough, when I need a more specific connection to what I have been listening to.",
    "The list seems to assume that recognizable albums and best-of collections are natural next choices, even though familiarity alone would not motivate me to interact."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several holiday albums appeared close together in my history, including a repeated title, which makes Christmas music a stronger clue than a general interest in popular music.",
    "My latest interaction with The New Old Fashioned adds a vocal-harmony connection; an album combining that with Christmas music gives me the clearest reason to choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in vocals, but only That's Christmas To Me brought together the holiday theme and harmonies that motivated my choice."
}
